hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16138","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Makki, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: A hadith reached me from a man who heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I bought a camel, then saddled it, and traveled to him a month until I came to him in Sham, and there was Abdullah ibn Unays. So I said to the doorkeeper: Tell him Jabir is at the door. He said: Ibn Abdullah? I said: Yes. So he came out trailing his garment, embraced me and I embraced him. So I said: A hadith reached me from you that you heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about retaliation, and I feared you die or I die before I hear it. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The people will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection, or he said: The servants, naked, uncircumcised, buhman. He said: We said: And what is buhman? He said: With them is nothing. Then He calls them with a voice heard from near: I am the King, I am the Requiter. And it befits no one of the people of Hell to enter Hell while he has with one of the people of Paradise a right, until I retaliate it from him. And it befits no one of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise while one of the people of Hell has with him a right, until I retaliate it from him, even the slap. He said: We said: How, while we come to Allah Almighty naked, uncircumcised, buhman? He said: With good deeds and evil deeds."
"16139","He said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh al-Taymi, from Abu Umamah al-Ansari, from Abdullah ibn Unays al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of the greatest of major sins are association with Allah, and disobedience to parents, and the drowning oath. And no swearer swears by Allah a binding oath, inserting in it even like a gnat wing, except Allah makes it a speck in his heart until the Day of Resurrection."
"16140","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar, meaning al-Makhrami, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Abdullah ibn Unays, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, and they asked him about a night they anticipate in Ramadan. He said: The night of twenty-three."
"16141","He said: Anas ibn Iyad Abu Damrah narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me, from Abu al-Nadr, the freedman of Umar ibn Ubaydillah, from Busr ibn Said, from Abdullah ibn Unays, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then I was made to forget it, and I saw myself in its morning prostrating in water and mud. So we were rained upon on the night of twenty-three, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us, and he left while the trace of water and mud was on his forehead and nose."
"16142","He said: Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb al-Juhani narrated to me, from his brother Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, he said: There was a man in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab who had asked him and he gave him. He said: Abdullah ibn Unays, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sat with us in his gathering, in the gathering of Juhaynah, in Ramadan. He said: So we said to him: O Abu Yahya, did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this blessed night anything? So he said: Yes, we sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the end of this month, and we said to him: O Messenger of Allah, when do we seek this blessed night? He said: Seek it this night. And he said: And that was the evening of the night of twenty-three. A man of the people said to him: And it is then, O Messenger of Allah, the first of eight? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not the first of eight, but it is the first of seven; the month does not complete."
"16143","He said: Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated, he said: From Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Ibn Abdullah ibn Unays, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: It has reached me that Khalid ibn Sufyan ibn Nubayh gathers the people against me to raid me, and he is at Uranah, so go to him and kill him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, describe him to me until I know him. He said: When you see him you will find for him a shudder. He said: So I went out girt with my sword until I came upon him, and he was at Uranah with women in litters, seeking for them a dwelling, and it was the time of Asr. When I saw him I found what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described to me of the shudder. So I came toward him, and I feared there would be between me and him a struggle that distracts me from prayer, so I prayed while walking toward him, gesturing with my head for bowing and prostration. When I reached him he said: Who is the man? I said: A man of the Arabs who heard of you and of your gathering against this man, and came to you for this. He said: Yes, I am about that. He said: So I walked with him a while, until when I was able, I struck him with the sword until I killed him, then I went out and left his women in litters bent over him. When I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he saw me, he said: The face has prospered. He said: I said: I killed him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You told truth. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with me and entered his house and gave me a staff, and said: Keep this with you, O Abdullah ibn Unays. He said: So I went out with it to the people, and they said: What is this staff? He said: I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave it to me and commanded me to keep it. They said: Will you not return to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him about that? He said: So I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you give me this staff? He said: A sign between me and you on the Day of Resurrection; the fewest of people on that day, the Day of Resurrection, are those leaning on staffs. So Abdullah joined it to his sword, and it remained with him until when he died he ordered with it and it was placed with him in his shroud, then they were buried together."
"16144","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from some of the children of Abdullah ibn Unays, from Abu Abdullah ibn Unays, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Khalid ibn Sufyan ibn Nubayh al-Hudhali to kill him, and he was gathering to fight the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I came to him at Uranah, and he was with his baggage, and the time of Asr had entered, and I feared there would be between me and him a struggle that distracts me from prayer. He said: So I prayed while walking, gesturing with gestures. When I reached him I said such and such, until he mentioned the hadith, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of his killing him, and mentioned the hadith."
